# Implementation Plan: Modular Persistence Layer & Data Management

## Goal
Transition QualiaQC from pickle-based state storage to a structured, modular SQLite database (via SQLAlchemy). This includes optimizing image/asset management in the [data](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/QualiaQC/src/project_management/manager.py#339-370) folder for production efficiency.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Database Modularization
#### [NEW] `src/db/base.py`
- Setup SQLAlchemy engine and session factory.
- Define a base class for all models.

#### [NEW] `src/db/models.py`
- Implement `AnalysisSession` (Metadata, config, status).
- Implement `AnalysisAsset` (Reference to physical files in [data/](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/QualiaQC/src/project_management/manager.py#339-370)).
- Implement `AnalysisMetric` (Structured results).

#### [NEW] `src/db/manager.py`
- Create a `DatabaseManager` class to encapsulate all DB operations (Modular CRUD).

### Data Folder Restructuring
#### [MODIFY] [src/config.py](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/QualiaQC/src/config.py)
- Update path constants to use a more structured [data/](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Coding/QualiaQC/src/project_management/manager.py#339-370) hierarchy (e.g., `data/projects`, `data/history/[UUID]/assets`).

#### [MODIFY] `src/project_management/manager.py`
- Integrate `DatabaseManager` for project-level state.
- Improve asset retrieval to search DB records instead of raw file iterations where appropriate.

### Pipeline Integration
#### [MODIFY] `src/pipeline.py`
- Replace `pickle.dump/load` in `save_state`/`load_state`.
- Ensure the pipeline registers every run as an `AnalysisSession`.

#### [MODIFY] `src/server.py`
- Update endpoints to query the DB for history and file statuses.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Create a test script `tests/test_persistence.py` to verify:
    - Session creation.
    - Asset linking.
    - Metric storage and retrieval.

### Manual Verification
1. Run a sample analysis.
2. Verify SQLite database contains the record.
3. Check `data/history/` for archived assets.
4. Regenerate a report using only the Session ID.
